{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\eng\\027.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Reading", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[156, 173], [334, 181], [332, 228], [154, 221]]}, {"text": "WhereIComeFrom", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[638, 210], [1164, 215], [1163, 259], [637, 253]]}, {"text": "Text28", "conf": 0.669, "box": [[84, 298], [194, 298], [194, 333], [84, 333]]}, {"text": "Read the poem by Elizabeth Brewster.She talks about nature and makes a small", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[148, 357], [1475, 358], [1475, 395], [148, 394]]}, {"text": "comparison between city and country life. Identify all the words and phrases that", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[147, 401], [1497, 405], [1496, 444], [147, 441]]}, {"text": "describe nature.", "conf": 0.844, "box": [[149, 445], [413, 449], [413, 483], [148, 479]]}, {"text": "People are made of places. They carry with them", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[195, 599], [998, 602], [998, 639], [194, 636]]}, {"text": "hints of jungles or mountains, a tropic grace", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[227, 653], [964, 659], [964, 699], [226, 693]]}, {"text": "or the cool eyes of sea gazers. Atmosphere of cities", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[169, 709], [1023, 713], [1023, 753], [168, 749]]}, {"text": "Points toknowl", "conf": 0.815, "box": [[1256, 736], [1490, 736], [1490, 766], [1256, 766]]}, {"text": "how different drops from them, like the smell of smog", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[145, 762], [1043, 769], [1042, 812], [144, 805]]}, {"text": "Poet uses language to", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[1190, 772], [1500, 775], [1499, 807], [1190, 804]]}, {"text": "or the almost-not-smell of tulips in the spring.", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[209, 819], [972, 827], [972, 867], [208, 859]]}, {"text": "conveyherexperience", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[1191, 815], [1503, 815], [1503, 845], [1191, 845]]}, {"text": "throughpoeticlanguage.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[1190, 854], [1542, 857], [1541, 888], [1190, 884]]}, {"text": "nature tidily plotted with a guidebook;", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[271, 881], [915, 881], [915, 921], [271, 921]]}, {"text": "Poetic language can be", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[1186, 892], [1515, 896], [1514, 929], [1186, 926]]}, {"text": "or the smell of work, glue factories maybe,", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[238, 935], [943, 939], [943, 978], [237, 974]]}, {"text": "created through the use", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[1188, 936], [1524, 936], [1524, 966], [1188, 966]]}, {"text": "of imagery and sound.", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[1188, 972], [1507, 974], [1506, 1010], [1188, 1008]]}, {"text": ". chromium-plated offices; smell of subways", "conf": 0.945, "box": [[219, 990], [944, 994], [944, 1034], [218, 1030]]}, {"text": "crowded at rush hours.", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[398, 1048], [780, 1050], [780, 1087], [398, 1085]]}, {"text": "Where I come from, people", "conf": 0.839, "box": [[357, 1157], [817, 1163], [817, 1205], [357, 1198]]}, {"text": "carry woods in their minds, acres of pine woods;", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[187, 1215], [990, 1219], [990, 1258], [186, 1255]]}, {"text": "blueberry patches in the burned-out bush;", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[231, 1272], [942, 1274], [942, 1314], [231, 1312]]}, {"text": "wooden farmhouses, old, in need of paint", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[233, 1329], [937, 1333], [937, 1369], [232, 1365]]}, {"text": "Points toknow!", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[1239, 1334], [1481, 1336], [1480, 1369], [1239, 1367]]}, {"text": "Think about the", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[1211, 1373], [1433, 1373], [1433, 1404], [1211, 1404]]}, {"text": "with yards where hens and chickens circle about,", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[181, 1386], [990, 1386], [990, 1426], [181, 1426]]}, {"text": "theme of the poem", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[1208, 1412], [1486, 1415], [1485, 1448], [1208, 1445]]}, {"text": "clucking aimlessly: battered schoolhouses", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[237, 1442], [934, 1444], [934, 1484], [237, 1482]]}, {"text": "and howthepoet", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[1209, 1457], [1464, 1457], [1464, 1487], [1209, 1487]]}, {"text": "behind which violets grow. Spring and winter", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[207, 1498], [962, 1502], [962, 1542], [206, 1537]]}, {"text": "makesanimpacton", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[1209, 1498], [1495, 1498], [1495, 1528], [1209, 1528]]}, {"text": "the reader through", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[1207, 1536], [1479, 1539], [1478, 1572], [1207, 1570]]}, {"text": "are the mind's chief seasons: ice and the breaking of ice.", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[115, 1554], [1050, 1559], [1049, 1595], [115, 1591]]}, {"text": "the choice of words.", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[1206, 1577], [1491, 1579], [1490, 1612], [1206, 1610]]}, {"text": "A door in the mind blows open, and there blows", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[177, 1669], [987, 1671], [987, 1707], [177, 1705]]}, {"text": "a frosty wind from fields of snow.", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[304, 1727], [858, 1727], [858, 1766], [304, 1766]]}, {"text": "(By:ElizabethWinifredBrewster)", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[948, 1816], [1395, 1816], [1395, 1846], [948, 1846]]}, {"text": "About the Poet:", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[39, 1872], [272, 1875], [271, 1905], [39, 1903]]}, {"text": "Elizabeth Winifred Brewster was a Canadian poet and a writer. She was born on 26 August 1922 and died at the", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[39, 1910], [1580, 1913], [1580, 1946], [39, 1943]]}, {"text": "age of 90 on 26 December 2012. Elizabeth Brewster has written more than 20 books, and most of them are poetry", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[37, 1947], [1605, 1951], [1605, 1988], [37, 1984]]}, {"text": "collections. Her first poem was published when was twelve years old. She was awarded with a number of life time", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[35, 1987], [1595, 1989], [1595, 2022], [35, 2020]]}, {"text": "achievementawards.", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[38, 2026], [327, 2026], [327, 2057], [38, 2057]]}, {"text": "22", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[789, 2133], [847, 2133], [847, 2177], [789, 2177]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.857, "box": [[153, 2177], [432, 2176], [432, 2211], [153, 2212]]}]}